# Secrets — never commit
*.env
.env
secrets/
secrets.env
*.ovpn
*_api_key*
*apikey*
*.pem
*.key

# Recon output / lab-specific (private repo territory). Subfoldered by
# content type (Machines/Sherlocks/Fortresses) purely for organization --
# the whole tree stays private, nothing here is ever un-ignored.
Recon Output/*
!Recon Output/.gitkeep

# Lab environment specifics (scope docs, VM inventory - often client-sensitive)
Lab Environment/*
!Lab Environment/.gitkeep

# CVE watch notes may reference active client context
CVE Watch/*
!CVE Watch/.gitkeep

# HTB Writeups: only RETIRED boxes may be public (see CLAUDE.md's
# Publishing rule). Subfoldered by content type (Machines/Sherlocks/
# Fortresses/Challenges). Nothing is un-ignored by default -- once a
# specific box is confirmed retired, add an explicit line below in the
# matching subfolder's block: "!HTB Writeups/Machines/<target>.md".
HTB Writeups/*
!HTB Writeups/.gitkeep
!HTB Writeups/Machines/
!HTB Writeups/Sherlocks/
!HTB Writeups/Fortresses/
!HTB Writeups/Challenges/

HTB Writeups/Machines/*
!HTB Writeups/Machines/.gitkeep
!HTB Writeups/Machines/fries.md
!HTB Writeups/Machines/kobold.md
!HTB Writeups/Machines/cobblestone.md

HTB Writeups/Sherlocks/*
!HTB Writeups/Sherlocks/.gitkeep

HTB Writeups/Fortresses/*
!HTB Writeups/Fortresses/.gitkeep

HTB Writeups/Challenges/*
!HTB Writeups/Challenges/.gitkeep

# Leftover disconnected Obsidian vault stub, not part of the real project
Security Guru/

# Orchestration/goal-tracking state — names active/in-progress targets before
# they're cleared for publishing; keep this private regardless of what's in
# HTB Writeups/. Structure preserved via .gitkeep; content excluded.
Orchestration/*
!Orchestration/.gitkeep
!Orchestration/queues/

# Paid third-party course material (OSAI+ etc.) — never public, no
# retired-content carve-out like HTB gets. CLAUDE.md has stated this
# unconditionally since it was added; this rule was missing until
# 2026-08-16 (found via a pre-push dry-run, nothing was ever actually
# pushed under the gap).
OffSec Labs/*
!OffSec Labs/.gitkeep

# Claude-independent local-model (Qwen) agent harness — a separate,
# still-evolving R&D project, not vault content. Likely graduates to its
# own repo later; excluded here in the meantime rather than left to ride
# along by accident (1.4GB+ as of 2026-08-16).
LLM Training/*
!LLM Training/.gitkeep

# Local app state, not vault content
.obsidian/
.claude/scratch/

# Cloud IAM privesc-graph engine — CLAUDE.md states this is private by
# default like every other folder here, un-ignored explicitly per file
# when ready to share (same pattern as HTB Writeups' retired-only rule).
# No file has been cleared for that yet. This rule was missing entirely
# until 2026-08-16 (found in the same pre-push gitignore audit).
Cloud Architecture/*
!Cloud Architecture/.gitkeep

# In-progress CTF challenge notes (standalone HTB Challenges + other CTF
# platforms) -- had no privacy rule at all until 2026-08-16, meaning this
# would have gone public wholesale on the next push. Applying this vault's
# own default-private/explicit-opt-in principle (Agent Operating
# Principles #7), same pattern as HTB Writeups: private by default,
# un-ignore a specific challenge's writeup explicitly once there's an
# actual reason to (e.g. a confirmed-retired HTB Challenge writeup drafted
# to HTB Writeups/Challenges/ -- the raw working notes/source dumps here
# stay private regardless). Found via a pre-push review after a real
# example (a full challenge source bundle + its actual flag value) was
# about to be swept in as a first-time oversight, not a decision.
CTF Notes/*
!CTF Notes/.gitkeep

# Third-party cloned repos pulled down during exploitation (ghostlink's
# Gogs instance) -- each carries its own nested .git, which breaks a
# clone of this outer repo if committed as-is (git itself warns: "adding
# embedded git repository"). Not ours to redistribute either way.
**/gogs-repos-clone/
